  "content": {
    "id": "p15-q14-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "14",
    "prompt": "The area of the triangle bounded by the lines $y=c+x$, $y=c-x$ and the $x$-axis is $9$. Find the value of $c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p15-q14-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "c=\\pm3",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p15-q14-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "The base is ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "2|c|",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": " and the height is ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "|c|",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ", so the area is ",
                "marks": []
              },
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "c^2",
                "display": false
              },
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": ".",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "Setting $y=0$ gives the intercepts $(-c,0)$ and $(c,0)$. The two lines meet at $(0,c)$, so the base is $2|c|$ and the perpendicular height is $|c|$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Area}&=\\frac12(2|c|)|c|\\\\\\text{Area}&=c^2\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}c^2&=9\\\\c&=\\pm3\\end{align*}$$\nBoth signs are possible: the triangle can lie above or below the $x$-axis.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
